{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q409375","formula":"ClH₂N","hill":"ClH2N","elements":["H","N","Cl"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"N":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Monochloramine","ru":"Хлорамин","uk":"Хлорамін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Monochloramine, often called chloramine, is the chemical compound with the formula NH2Cl. Together with dichloramine (NHCl2) and nitrogen trichloride (NCl3), it is one of the three chloramines of ammonia. It is a colorless liquid at its melting point of −66 °C (−87 °F), but it is usually handled as a dilute aqueous solution, and it is sometimes used as a disinfectant in this form.","ru":"Хлорами́н — неорганическое соединение, хлорпроизводное аммиака с формулой NH2Cl, бесцветная маслянистая жидкость, растворимая в холодной воде, разлагается при температурах выше −40 °C.","uk":"Хлорамін, або монохлорамін — хімічна сполука з формулою NH2Cl. Разом з дихлораміном (NHCl2) і трихлоридом азоту (NCl3) він є одним із трьох хлорамінів аміаку. Це безбарвна рідина з температурою плавлення −66 °C (−87 °F)."},"fame":31,"pubchemCid":25423,"mass":51.47,"charge":0,"smiles":"NCl","inchikey":"QDHHCQZDFGDHMP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"25423","atoms":4,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.88,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.88,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":1.236,"y":-0.807,"z":-0.511,"el":"H"},{"x":1.236,"y":-0.091,"z":0.951,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[1,2,1],[1,3,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409375","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monochloramine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0%D0